sequenceDiagram
  autonumber

  participant C as Client
  participant BR as Kafka broker
  participant A as Kafka agent

  Note over C,A: Kafka A2A transport — three interaction patterns<br/>Same topics · compare below · one per task, not concurrent

  rect rgb(238, 243, 248)
    Note over C,A: Pattern 1 — Request/response · short path, one logical result
    C->>BR: produce message/send → a2a.requests
    BR->>A: consume request
    A->>BR: produce artifact-update → a2a.updates
    A->>BR: produce status-update COMPLETED
    A->>BR: produce task snapshot
    BR->>C: consume until terminal
  end

  rect rgb(245, 248, 252)
    Note over C,A: Pattern 2 — Streaming · many ordered events over time
    C->>BR: produce message/send → a2a.requests
    BR->>A: consume request
    A->>BR: produce status-update WORKING
    loop Multiple chunks over time
      A->>BR: produce artifact-update
      BR->>C: consume chunk
    end
    A->>BR: produce status-update COMPLETED
    BR->>C: consume final
    Note over C: Kafka consumer replaces HTTP SSE on this binding
  end

  rect rgb(238, 243, 248)
    Note over C,A: Pattern 3 — Notifications · async observer (not HTTP webhook)
    C->>BR: produce message/send → a2a.requests
    BR->>A: consume request
    A->>BR: produce status-update WORKING
    A->>BR: produce artifact-update
    A->>BR: produce status-update COMPLETED
    BR->>C: consume when ready
    Note over C: Same a2a.updates topic as stream — no POST to client URL
  end
